Upgrade procedure for xz

XZ Utils is a general-purpose data compression package with a high
compression ratio, built around the LZMA2 algorithm.

Website: https://tukaani.org/xz/
Source:  https://github.com/tukaani-project/xz/releases/download/vVERSION/xz-VERSION.tar.gz
	 (check the .sig next to it; signing key
	 3690C240CE51B4670D30AD1C38EE757D69184620, Lasse Collin)

To upgrade to a new version:

1. Download, verify and extract the tarball to /tmp/xz/xz-VERSION.
2. Use the vendor-update skill (vendor/xz/dist, contrib/xz, tag
   vendor/xz/dist/VERSION).  Prune the files in MIDNIGHTBSD-Xlist from
   the extracted tree before staging; the vendor branch is trimmed.
3. After the subtree merge, update PACKAGE_STRING, PACKAGE_VERSION and
   VERSION in lib/liblzma/config.h.  Compare config.h.in in the
   tarball with lib/liblzma/config.h and add any new macros.
   FreeBSD's lib/liblzma/config.h is a useful reference.
4. Check lib/liblzma/Makefile and usr.bin/xz/Makefile against new or
   removed sources.
5. Build lib/liblzma, usr.bin/xz, usr.bin/xzdec and usr.bin/lzmainfo.

Local changes on top of upstream:

  - src/common/w32_application.manifest,
    src/common/w32_application.manifest.comments.txt and
    src/liblzma/check/sha256.c are on the vendor branch but removed
    in-tree (since xz 5.6.3).  liblzma uses libmd's SHA-256 instead of
    the bundled one (see lib/liblzma/Makefile).  If a merge brings them
    back, git rm them again.

Notes:
  - ChangeLog is the one shipped in the tarball.
